  "summary": "Malicious code in @onereach/bandwidth-steps-voice-bxml (npm)",
  "details": "The package runs a preinstall hook (node setup.mjs) that downloads the Bun JavaScript runtime and executes a 727KB heavily-obfuscated payload (math_init.js) at install time. The payload uses a custom string-array decoder with high-entropy obfuscation, making its behaviour opaque to static inspection while it runs during installation. This is a multi-stage dropper pattern: a small install hook fetches a runtime and then executes an obfuscated second-stage payload on the installer's machine.",
